INT. CLOSED ICE-CREAM PARLOR - BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Pastel walls and a dead freezer. A single bulb. VINCENT "VINNIE" DELACORTE (50s, suit, tie loosened) sits at a small table. Across from him, DETECTIVE MARGARET "MAGS" OYELARAN (40s, gray blazer) turns a sundae spoon over in her fingers.

                    VINNIE
          You came alone.

                    MAGS
          I did.

                    VINNIE
          (to the empty room)
          Somebody always comes alone.

He pours himself coffee from a thermos and slides a second cup across. She does not touch it. He drinks. The silence stretches.

                    VINNIE (CONT'D)
          You know what I miss? The chocolate chip.

                    MAGS
          Is that right.

                    VINNIE
          My mother worked here. Thirty years behind that counter.

Mags sets down the spoon. She studies his hands, which are not quite steady.

A door opens at the rear. A thin YOUNG LAWYER (20s, rain-soaked briefcase) slips in, looks from one to the other, and stops.

                    YOUNG LAWYER
          Mr. Delacorte, I told you not to speak without--

                    VINNIE
          Sit, Peter. The detective and I are only talking about ice cream.

Peter sits. Mags stands, puts a card on the table, and tucks the spoon into her coat pocket.

                    MAGS
          (to the room)
          Nobody leaves town.

She goes out. Vinnie stares at the cup she never touched, then slowly drinks it himself.
